---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Start Here: The Indian Investor Roadmap — Artha Atlas"
  description="The foundational step-by-step financial sequence for Indian citizens: insurance fortress, emergency fund, debt elimination, asset allocation, and tax-efficient compounding."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Start Here: The Investor Roadmap' }]} />

    <header class="my-6 pb-6 border-b border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/60 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-900 px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3">
        <span>🧭 Step-by-Step Sequence</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Foundational Protocol</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-50 tracking-tight leading-tight">
        The Indian Investor Roadmap
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 mt-3 font-sans leading-relaxed">
        Before risking a single rupee in the equity market or speculative derivatives, you must build an unassailable balance sheet fortress. Here is the mathematically optimal sequence.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-12">
      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-600 text-white font-serif font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">
            1
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
            Build the Catastrophic Insurance Shield
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
          The single biggest destroyer of middle-class wealth in India is unexpected healthcare expenditure. Before investing in equities, secure two non-negotiable insurance pillars:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">
              🏥 Comprehensive Health Cover
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              Never rely solely on your employer’s corporate policy. Buy an individual/family floater base plan of ₹10–15 Lakhs + a Super Top-up policy of ₹50–90 Lakhs with a ₹10 Lakh deductible.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800">
            <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 mb-1">
              🛡️ Pure Term Life Insurance
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
              If anyone is financially dependent on your income, purchase a pure term policy covering 15–20x of your annual expenses. Strictly avoid ULIPs and endowment plans.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <Callout type="warning" title="The Endowment & ULIP Trap">
          Never mix insurance with investment. Traditional life insurance policies (LIC endowment, money-back, ULIPs) yield a miserable 4.5%–6.0% return while locking capital for decades. Buy pure term insurance and invest the difference in mutual funds.
        </Callout>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-600 text-white font-serif font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">
            2
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
            Establish a 6-to-12 Month Emergency Fund
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
          Calculate your non-negotiable monthly outflow: rent/EMI, groceries, utility bills, insurance premiums, and school fees. Multiply by 6 (or 12 if you are in a volatile sector or self-employed).
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
          Park this capital across two high-liquidity, zero-drawdown buckets:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-xs sm:text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>50% in Bank Sweep-in FDs:</strong> Linked to your primary savings account for instant ATM/UPI withdrawal access.</li>
          <li><strong>50% in Liquid / Overnight Mutual Funds:</strong> Held in Tier-1 AMCs investing exclusively in sovereign and AAA papers with instant redemption up to ₹50,000.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-600 text-white font-serif font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">
            3
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
            Eliminate High-Interest Unsecured Debt
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
          Credit cards charge 36%–42% annualized interest. Personal loans cost 13%–18%. No equity fund or quant algorithm on earth can out-compound a 40% negative compounding liability. Pay off every rupee of unsecured debt immediately.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-600 text-white font-serif font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-sm">
            4
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
            Deploy via Goal-Based Asset Allocation
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
          Never invest without matching the instrument to the time horizon:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-3 pt-2">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-900 flex justify-between items-center text-xs">
            <div>
              <strong class="font-serif text-sm block text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Short-Term Goals (&lt; 3 Years)</strong>
              <span class="text-stone-500">Vacation, wedding, upcoming tax liability, car purchase</span>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right font-medium text-amber-600">
              100% Fixed Income (T-Bills, Arbitrage Funds, Bank FDs)
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-900 flex justify-between items-center text-xs">
            <div>
              <strong class="font-serif text-sm block text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Medium-Term Goals (3 – 7 Years)</strong>
              <span class="text-stone-500">Home down-payment, sabbatical capital</span>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right font-medium text-amber-600">
              40% Equity / 50% Debt / 10% Gold (Multi-Asset / Conservative Hybrid)
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-900 flex justify-between items-center text-xs">
            <div>
              <strong class="font-serif text-sm block text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Long-Term Wealth & FIRE (&gt; 7 Years)</strong>
              <span class="text-stone-500">Retirement corpus, multi-decade compounding</span>
            </div>
            <div class="text-right font-medium text-amber-600">
              70–80% Diversified Equity / 15% Debt / 5–10% Gold
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Next Steps -->
      <div class="pt-8 border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
            Ready to explore specific instruments?
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-stone-500">
            Compare all 40+ investment vehicles in our single-source-of-truth directory.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href={`${base}/avenues/`}
          class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-amber-600 hover:bg-amber-700 text-white font-medium text-xs shadow-sm transition-all whitespace-nowrap"
        >
          Explore All Avenues →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
